  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of lifesaving essential health services to displaced people and vulnerable host communities in Rakhine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide lifesaving essential health services in Rakhine. This UNICEF project provides 1) 6,000 primary health care consultations, 2) essential medical treatments for chronic diseases to 2,400 people, 3) antenatal care services to 1,000 pregnant women and 4)  essential medical treatments to 6,000 infants. The project provides life-saving assistance to 10,000 people, including 4,500 women, 3,600 men, 19,000 children, and 500 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
